Most of these are priors, not measurements: I didn't run anything against NAS-Bench-201. The numbers come from general knowledge of the benchmark: nor_conv_3x3 is usually the strongest op, and removing a path through node 2 or node 1 matters more when that path carries a convolution. They also rest on rough reasoning about which paths in the cell carry signal.

The most confident calls are same-edge conditions where the parent op is nor_conv_3x3 (claims 4, 8, 9, 13). Replacing the best op loses accuracy, so the edit's effect should be lower under that condition, and those claims get low numbers. Most cross-edge claims sit near 50 because I have no strong reason to expect a consistent interaction across all three datasets.

